Document.description_en:
Zagime Anishinabek is proposing a mix of both large and small format commercial tenants, medium and high-density mixed-use residential areas, and additional multi-unit residential buildings on the urban reserve of Saulteaux Junction Zagime IR No. 74-6. The proposed project is called Sage Meadow Development and will cover approximately 280 acres. Sage Meadow Development will utilize the existing systems on the property and tie in new service connections. The site is currently undeveloped agricultural land and project will be completed in phases. An existing gas station and two commercial buildings are located along the east side of the subject property. The remainder of the site consists of cultivated farmland.

&nbsp;

Phase1A will require roadwork and site preparation, trench excavation and backfill, pressure pipe domestic sewer, building services, utilities. Utilities currently identified on site are: Power lines, Buried electrical cable, buried or overhead phone cable, low pressure gas utility, buried sanitary sewer, buried storm sewer, buried water line.

&nbsp;

Approximately 1,190 m of roadways, including the reconstruction of Three Sisters Avenue to an urban collector cross-section, and intersection improvements at Dewdney Avenue and Pinkie Road, including turn lanes and traffic signals.

Document.description_fr:
Zagime Anishinabek propose un m&eacute;lange de locataires commerciaux de grand et petit format, de zones r&eacute;sidentielles mixtes de moyenne et haute densit&eacute;, ainsi que d&#39;autres immeubles r&eacute;sidentiels multi-unit&eacute;s dans la r&eacute;serve urbaine de Saulteaux Junction Zagime IR no 74-6. Le projet propos&eacute; s&#39;appelle Sage Meadow Development et couvrira environ 280 acres. Sage Meadow Development utilisera les syst&egrave;mes existants sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; et reliera de nouvelles connexions de service. Le site est actuellement un terrain agricole non d&eacute;velopp&eacute; et le projet sera compl&eacute;t&eacute; par phases. Une station-service existante et deux b&acirc;timents commerciaux se trouvent le long du c&ocirc;t&eacute; est de la propri&eacute;t&eacute; concern&eacute;e. Le reste du site est constitu&eacute; de terres agricoles cultiv&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

La phase 1A n&eacute;cessitera des travaux routiers et la pr&eacute;paration du site, l&#39;excavation de tranch&eacute;es et le remblai, des &eacute;gouts domestiques sous pression, des services de construction, des services publics. Les services publics actuellement identifi&eacute;s sur le site sont : lignes &eacute;lectriques, c&acirc;ble &eacute;lectrique enfoui, c&acirc;ble t&eacute;l&eacute;phonique enseveli ou a&eacute;rien, service de gaz basse pression, &eacute;gouts sanitaires enterr&eacute;s, &eacute;gouts pluviaux enterr&eacute;s, conduites d&#39;eau enfouies.

&nbsp;

Environ 1 190 m de routes, incluant la reconstruction de Three Sisters Avenue en section transversale urbaine, ainsi que des am&eacute;liorations aux intersections &agrave; Dewdney Avenue et Pinkie Road, incluant des voies de virage et des feux de circulation.

