Document.description_en:
The Proposed Project: Laydown and Logistics areas&nbsp;

As part of the Greater Toronto Airports Authority&#39;s (GTAA&#39;s) Toronto Pearson Airport Longterm Investment in Facilities &amp; Terminals (LIFT) Program,&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;and laydown areas will be constructed on Airport Lands, to&nbsp;facilitate&nbsp;construction needs.&nbsp;These sites will be developed on&nbsp;unmaintained&nbsp;vegetated&nbsp;areas&nbsp;located&nbsp;both airside and groundside&nbsp;on&nbsp;airport&nbsp;property.&nbsp;The sites will consist of&nbsp;a combination of any of the following:&nbsp;temporary construction trailers, worker parking lot, material laydown, equipment storage, and associated infrastructure to support Airport construction projects.&nbsp;

The sites will undergo a variety of improvements, depending on&nbsp;the current conditions and&nbsp;the requirements for construction.&nbsp;Activities may include, as&nbsp;required,&nbsp;vegetation removal,&nbsp;minor excavation, clearing and grubbing, utility removals /relocations including the addition of temporary pole-mounted lighting with overhead power, re-grading , placement of aggregate and compact areas where required, construction trailers, security booths, transportation services for workers, paving and line painting of parking and trailer areas, stormwater management, and other associated infrastructure. No new permanent buildings are proposed. Trailers will be prefabricated units delivered to the site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Several sustainability best practices will be incorporated into the projects design and implementation for the wider Toronto Pearson Airport Longterm Investment in Facilities &amp; Terminals (LIFT) Program.

Document.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; : zones de stockage et de logistique&nbsp;

Dans le cadre du&nbsp;programme&nbsp;d&#39;investissement&nbsp;&agrave; long&nbsp;terme&nbsp;dans les installations et les&nbsp;terminaux&nbsp;(LIFT) de&nbsp;l&#39;Autorit&eacute;&nbsp;des&nbsp;a&eacute;roports&nbsp;du Grand Toronto&nbsp;(GTAA) &agrave;&nbsp;l&#39;a&eacute;roport&nbsp;Toronto Pearson, des zones de logistique et de stockage seront am&eacute;nag&eacute;es sur les terrains de l&#39;a&eacute;roport afin de r&eacute;pondre aux besoins de construction.&nbsp;Ces sites seront d&eacute;velopp&eacute;s sur des zones v&eacute;g&eacute;talis&eacute;es non entretenues situ&eacute;es &agrave; la fois c&ocirc;t&eacute; piste et c&ocirc;t&eacute; terre sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; de l&#39;a&eacute;roport. Les sites comprendront une combinaison de l&#39;un quelconque des &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants : des roulottes de&nbsp;chantier temporaires, un parking pour les travailleurs, un d&eacute;p&ocirc;t de mat&eacute;riaux, un stockage de mat&eacute;riel et l&#39;infrastructure associ&eacute;e pour soutenir les projets de construction de l&#39;a&eacute;roport.&nbsp;

Les sites subiront une vari&eacute;t&eacute; d&#39;am&eacute;liorations, en fonction des conditions actuelles et des exigences de construction. Les activit&eacute;s peuvent inclure, selon les besoins, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation, des excavations mineures, le d&eacute;blaiement et le d&eacute;frichage, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement ou le d&eacute;placement des services publics, y compris l&#39;ajout d&#39;un &eacute;clairage temporaire sur poteaux avec alimentation &eacute;lectrique a&eacute;rienne, le&nbsp;re-nivellement, la pose d&#39;agr&eacute;gats et le compactage des zones si n&eacute;cessaire, l&#39;installation de bureaux mobiles, de kiosques de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, des services de transport pour les travailleurs, le pavage et le marquage des zones de stationnement et des zones de bureaux mobiles, la gestion des eaux pluviales et d&#39;autres infrastructures associ&eacute;es. Aucun nouveau b&acirc;timent permanent n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu. Les bureaux mobiles seront des unit&eacute;s pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;es livr&eacute;es sur le site.&nbsp;

Les&nbsp;meilleures&nbsp;pratiques&nbsp;en&nbsp;mati&egrave;re de&nbsp;durabilit&eacute;&nbsp;seront&nbsp;int&eacute;gr&eacute;es&nbsp;&agrave; la&nbsp;fois&nbsp;dans les phases de conception et de construction,&nbsp;en&nbsp;alignement&nbsp;avec le&nbsp;programme&nbsp;plus large&nbsp;d&#39;investissement&nbsp;&agrave; long&nbsp;terme&nbsp;dans les installations et&nbsp;terminaux&nbsp;(LIFT) de&nbsp;l&#39;a&eacute;roport&nbsp;Toronto Pearson.&nbsp;

